        "text": "Kevin John Olickal formerly served as executive director of the Indo-American Democratic Organization.",
        "cites": [1, 2]
      },
      {
        "text": "Olickal is the chief House sponsor of the Responsibility in Firearms Legislation Act. The bill would require gun manufacturers to pay into a state fund based on how many of their firearms are recovered from shootings in Illinois. He sponsored the Warehouse Worker Protection Act, which passed the legislature but was vetoed by the governor. His bills that became law include a measure on general assistance in townships. He also sponsored a law on consumer electronics recycling.",
